1
00:03:10,588 --> 00:03:16,588
Guess who's coming to save the world again?

2
00:06:21,176 --> 00:06:27,176
Ghostbusters II is a comedy, fantasy film directed by Ivan Reitman.

3
00:09:31,764 --> 00:09:37,764
The discovery of a massive river of ectoplasm and a resurgence of spectral
activity allows the staff of Ghostbusters to revive the business.

4
00:12:42,352 --> 00:12:48,352
Peter Venkman, played by Bill Murray.

5
00:15:52,941 --> 00:15:58,941
Ray Stantz, played by Dan Aykroyd.

6
00:19:03,529 --> 00:19:09,529
Dana Barrett, played by Sigourney Weaver.

7
00:22:14,117 --> 00:22:20,117
Dr. Egon Spengler, played by Harold Ramis.

8
00:25:24,705 --> 00:25:30,705
Louis Tully, played by Rick Moranis.

9
00:28:35,294 --> 00:28:41,294
Winston Zeddemore, played by Ernie Hudson.

10
00:31:45,882 --> 00:31:51,882
Ghostbusters II is a 1989 American supernatural comedy film directed by
Ivan Reitman and written by Dan Aykroyd and Harold Ramis.

11
00:34:56,470 --> 00:35:02,470
The film stars Bill Murray, Aykroyd, Sigourney Weaver, Ramis,
Rick Moranis, Ernie Hudson, and Annie Potts.

12
00:38:07,058 --> 00:38:13,058
It is the sequel to the 1984 film Ghostbusters and the
second film in the Ghostbusters franchise.

13
00:41:17,647 --> 00:41:23,647
Set five years after the events of the first film, the Ghostbusters have been sued and put out of
business after the destruction caused during their battle with the deity Gozer the Gozerian.

14
00:44:28,235 --> 00:44:34,235
When a new paranormal threat emerges, the Ghostbusters
reunite to combat it and save the world.

15
00:47:38,823 --> 00:47:44,823
After the success of Ghostbusters, Columbia Pictures wanted a sequel but
struggled to overcome objections from the cast and crew.

16
00:50:49,411 --> 00:50:55,411
As with the first film, Aykroyd and Ramis collaborated on the
script, which went through many variations.

17
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The pair wanted to convey a message about the consequences
of negative human emotions in large cities.

18
00:57:10,588 --> 00:57:16,588
They settled on the idea of negative feelings creating a mass of supernatural
slime beneath New York City that empowers malevolent spirits.

19
01:00:21,176 --> 01:00:27,176
With a budget of $30–40 million, filming took place between November
1988 and March 1989 in New York City and Los Angeles.

20
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
Production was rushed and large sections of the film were
scrapped after poorly received test screenings.

21
01:06:42,352 --> 01:06:48,352
New scenes were written and filmed during re-shoots between March
and April 1989, only two months before its release.

22
01:09:52,941 --> 01:09:58,941
Ghostbusters II was released on June 16, 1989, to generally negative reviews.

23
01:13:03,529 --> 01:13:09,529
Critics responded unfavorably to what they perceived as largely a copy of the original and a softening of its cynical, dark humor to be
more family-friendly, although the performances of Peter MacNicol and Rick Moranis were repeatedly singled out for praise.

24
01:16:14,117 --> 01:16:20,117
As the sequel to the then-highest-grossing comedy film of all time,
Ghostbusters II was expected to dominate the box office.

25
01:19:24,705 --> 01:19:30,705
Instead, the film earned $215.4 million during its theatrical run compared with the
original's $282.2 million, making it the eighth-highest-grossing film of the year.

26
01:22:35,294 --> 01:22:41,294
Columbia Pictures deemed it a failure, effectively dissuading
Murray from participating in a third Ghostbusters film.

27
01:25:45,882 --> 01:25:51,882
Its soundtrack single, "On Our Own" by Bobby Brown, was a success,
spending 20 weeks on the United States music charts.

28
01:28:56,470 --> 01:29:02,470
The film failed to replicate the cultural impact and following of Ghostbusters and was seen as
responsible for stalling the franchise for decades, though its reception has improved over time.

29
01:32:07,058 --> 01:32:13,058
The film spawned a series of merchandise including video games, board
games, comic books, music, toys, and haunted houses.

30
01:35:17,647 --> 01:35:23,647
Despite the relative failure of Ghostbusters II, a second
sequel was pursued through to the early 2010s.

31
01:38:28,235 --> 01:38:34,235
Following the mixed reviews and financial underperformance of the 2016 series reboot, the series returned to the
original film canon with Ghostbusters: Afterlife (2021) and Ghostbusters: Frozen Empire (2024).

32
01:41:38,823 --> 01:41:44,823
The film explores themes of new year's eve, new york
city, painting, supernatural, ghostbuster.

33
01:44:49,411 --> 01:44:55,411
The tone is lighthearted.
